  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inventory study on horticulture in the Rabat-Sal&#xE9;-K&#xE9;nitra and Larache region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Morocco is one of the leading producers of fruits and vegetables in North Africa, both for domestic use and for export. The country faces a major challenge due to water scarcity and the current cultivation methods. New, sustainable cultivation techniques are needed, including more efficient water use, higher yields and sustainable production, including the use of pesticides.There is a lot of interest from Moroccan stakeholders in Dutch knowledge and technology, as well as the Dutch model of triple helix cooperation. On the other hand, there is a lot of interest from the Dutch business community in the Moroccan horticultural sector, especially in the Rabat-Sal&#xE9;-K&#xE9;nitra and Larache region.An inventory study is being carried out to integrate sustainable Dutch knowledge and technology into the horticultural sector in the Rabat-Sal&#xE9;-K&#xE9;nitra and Larache region.This study will identify available Dutch technologies, as well as Moroccan and Dutch parties that can and want to contribute to the sustainable improvement of the horticultural sector in this region.</narrative>
  </description>
